From 58810d879189f9ee9730f8927d6ae73b7eb244d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luannt <luannt.devops@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 23:42:29 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agent): MCP instructions only for agents that have that
 server's tools

Every turn got the <mcp-instructions> of every connected MCP server, including
sub-agents, agentic_fetch and plan, which have no MCP tools at all (the same
failure Context Mode hit in #233: global tool availability is not the current
agent's capability). mcpInstructions now takes the request's tool set and only
includes servers with a tool in it; the resource tools reach any server, so an
agent that has them still gets all instructions and the main agent's prompt is
unchanged. Servers are emitted in sorted order, so with two or more servers the
system prompt no longer changes between turns (provider prompt cache).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
